From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 25/66] treewide: reconnect to ubus when ubusd restarts

When ubusd restarts, most of its clients stay off ubus until they are
restarted themselves: libubus' default connection_lost does nothing
once uloop has dropped the hung-up socket, so a daemon on it runs on
disconnected and procd never respawns it. Killing ubusd left 20 of 36
objects on a W-118 and on a C-260: LuCI (rpcd) stopped working, and
dnsmasq, odhcpd and odhcp6c were gone from ubus. Package patches, one
per project, for upstream each:

- rpcd: reconnect once a second; ubus_reconnect() registers the
  objects again.
- odhcpd: the same, and renew the ubus.object.add event and the
  network.interface subscription (the object has a new ID).
- odhcp6c: it freed the context on a failed reconnect while the main
  loop still held it (polling a stale fd, then a double free on exit);
  keep it, and reconnect from the main loop once a second.
- dnsmasq: it freed the context inside libubus' callback, and only
  retried when poll() happened to wake; drop it after the callback,
  wake every quarter second while disconnected, and reset the
  dnsmasq.dns object's IDs (on top of 200-ubus_dns.patch).
- procd: ujail -u bound the socket file, so a jailed dnsmasq or ntpd
  stayed on the dead ubusd's socket for good; bind the /var/run/ubus
  directory, read-only.

Bump each PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
